    "desiredJobDescription": "I'd like to live in one of the big players of the industry as a UX Designer\n\n",
    "goodPractices": "---\n\nI like doing things well and keeping them simple. I come from product design, but I work close to code, so most of my practice sits between design and engineering.\n\nThe main thing for me right now is AI. Most of my prototyping runs through it, and I've built a fair few projects with Claude Code, from small internal tools to working web apps and design experiments. It's changed how I work. I go from an idea to something you can click on in an afternoon, so I test more, throw away more, and keep only what holds up. I try to stay honest about the results too, not just show the demo that happened to work.\n\nI know how to work with design systems to build consistent experiences. I lean on them properly, follow the patterns, and use tools like Storybook so everyone works from the same source and the result stays coherent. It's the Clean Code idea, just applied to interfaces instead of functions.\n\nAnd accessibility is always in there. I'm the person my team goes to for it, and I treat WCAG as the starting point, not something you bolt on at the end.\n\nI keep learning too. The tools move quickly, and you can't really stop at whatever worked last year."
  }
